  "question": {
    "text": "Let a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> be concentric to the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>285</mn></math>. Then the common tangents are inclined to the minor axis of the ellipse at the angle",
    "image": null
  },
